    {
      "id": 171381,
      "name": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
      "username": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/{size}/1967_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-04-04T10:30:06.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Playing the cardboard game, my intuition always told me that if there wasn't a target next to an attachable card, it ought to go away. But with TUT, it's actually useful to keep it in play; if it's your only bounty, you can still get use out of the Masadah and Danny Boy, if DR is an issue. Granted, it still seems like a weird thing, but that's the only reason I can see for it staying in play. (Unless we want to get into discussions of it being his \"best\" bounty.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>As far as I remember from playtesting, the reason for leaving that text off was partially that fitting the text on the card was tricky, and partially thematic - it's the&nbsp;<em>ultimate&nbsp;</em>target, after all, so it shouldn't be being thrown all over the place as easily. Plus it still powers Hunter and Hunted, Masadah, etc. which is gravy.</p>",
